@namespace SpaceSails.Client.Pages
@implements IHandleEvent
@*
    #251 · THE SPREAD, ON ITS OWN FILE.

    THE PAPERS, OUT ON THE TABLE. The seated half of the case: the dig that files a sheet into the
    book (#784), and the reconcile that lays two of them side by side and prints what the table said
    (#973 L3). Every word of the three verdicts is Core's; this block lays a row and shows it.

    Moved out of SatchelPanel.razor by PURE MOTION — the block between the two fences below is the block
    that was in the panel, character for character. Every member it reads is a [Parameter] with the SAME
    NAME (a field keeps its underscore, a method arrives as a delegate under its own name, a variable the
    panel's `@if` bound arrives under the name that binding gave it), which is what lets the markup move
    without a rewrite and lets the composition splice it straight back where it came from.

    IHandleEvent repeats SatchelPanel's own override, which repeats Map.Sim.cs's: the HUD's refresh
    belongs to OnTick's 200 ms throttle, and a child that did not repeat it would put an automatic render
    back on every event in here. The .razor.css beside this file carries the four rule blocks of the
    satchel's sheet that THIS markup, and no other component in the client, renders (#1166); its scope
    is the PAGE's own (b-4dqsdx4p75, pinned in SpaceSails.Client.csproj), so every rule — the ones
    beside it and the shared kit left in SatchelPanel.razor.css — goes on matching it.

    The `@{ }` around the fences is not decoration: the block came out of a Razor CODE block, and a code
    block is where its first statements are legal. It is outside the fences, so what the composition reads
    is exactly the lines that stood in the panel.
*@
@{
@* ── MARKUP BEGINS · verbatim from SatchelPanel.razor ────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
                    <div class="satchel-sub">@(CaseHasBegun ? SpaceSails.Core.SeatedSpread.SpreadAgainBlurb : SpaceSails.Core.SeatedSpread.SpreadBlurb)</div>

                    @if (_satchelOutcome is { Length: > 0 } spreadSaid)
                    {
                        <div class="satchel-outcome">@spreadSaid</div>
                    }
                    else if (SpreadRefusal is { Length: > 0 } spreadNo)
                    {
                        <div class="satchel-outcome">@spreadNo</div>
                    }

                    @if (ProcessingUnderway() is { } spreadBusy)
                    {
                        <div class="satchel-outcome">@spreadBusy</div>
                    }

                    @* ── #973 L3 · THE RECONCILE. The other verb a table full of paper is for: lay two
                       things side by side and see whether they are talking about the same world. Every
                       word of the three verdicts is Fable's (SpreadReconcile); this markup lays a row and
                       prints what the table said.

                       The laid pair is drawn ABOVE the papers, because it is what the captain is looking
                       at — and the second question sits under the verdict rather than beside it, since it
                       is a count and not a conclusion. Nothing here is disabled (#212/#603): a paper
                       already on the table says so on its own row. *@
                    @if (LayablePapers() is { Count: > 0 } papers)
                    {
                        <div class="spread-lay">
                            <div class="satchel-sub">
                                @SpaceSails.Core.SeatedSpread.LayThemTogetherBlurb
                            </div>

                            @if (_laid.Count > 0)
                            {
                                <div class="spread-laid">
                                    @foreach (SpaceSails.Core.SpreadReconcile.Paper on in _laid)
                                    {
                                        <span class="spread-laid-item">@on.Label</span>
                                    }
                                    <button type="button" class="satchel-filter"
                                            title="Take everything off the table"
                                            @onclick="ClearTheSpread">✕</button>
                                </div>
                            }

                            @if (_reconciled is { } said)
                            {
                                <div class="satchel-outcome spread-verdict">@said.Line</div>
                                <div class="spread-second-question">@said.SecondQuestion</div>
                            }

                            <div class="satchel-items">
                                @foreach (SpaceSails.Core.SpreadReconcile.Paper paper in papers)
                                {
                                    SpaceSails.Core.SpreadReconcile.Paper lay = paper;
                                    <div class="satchel-row">
                                        <button type="button" class="satchel-item spread-item"
                                                title="@SpaceSails.Core.SeatedSpread.LayItHint"
                                                @onclick="() => LayItOnTheSpread(lay)">
                                            <span class="satchel-item-name">@paper.Label</span>
                                            <span class="satchel-item-try">
                                                @(IsLaid(paper.Id)
                                                    ? SpaceSails.Core.SeatedSpread.AlreadyLaidWord
                                                    : SpaceSails.Core.SeatedSpread.LayItWord)
                                            </span>
                                        </button>
                                    </div>
                                }
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    }

                    @if (SpreadableFinds() is { Count: > 0 } spreadable)
                    {
                        <div class="satchel-items">
                            @foreach (SpaceSails.Core.Satchel.Item lying in spreadable)
                            {
                                SpaceSails.Core.Satchel.Item dig = lying;
                                <div class="satchel-row">
                                    @* Through SpreadDigClicked and not WriteItUp directly: a successful
                                       press CLOSES this dialog (#696 shuts the pocket so the deck comes
                                       back), and a click that closes a dialog leaves focus on a button that
                                       no longer exists — the map then takes no keys at all. Found by
                                       playing it. *@
                                    <button type="button" class="satchel-item spread-item"
                                            title="@WriteUpHint(dig)"
                                            @onclick="() => SpreadDigClicked(dig)">
                                        <span class="satchel-item-name">@SatchelLabel(dig)</span>
                                        <span class="satchel-item-try">
                                            @SpaceSails.Core.SeatedPosture.WriteGlyph @SpreadRowVerb(dig)
                                        </span>
                                    </button>
                                    @* #798 · …AND THE OTHER END OF THE EVENING. Owner: "those trash cans
                                       are needed so we get rid of the processed materials without
                                       connecting them to us too clearly, like leaving them to the table."
                                       The loop is sit, dig, book, BIN — and the bin has to be on the page
                                       the digging happened on, or the last rung is somewhere else.

                                       Never disabled: with no bin within reach it says so, on this page,
                                       and names what would fix it. *@
                                    @if (RipIsOffered(dig))
                                    {
                                        <button type="button" class="satchel-leave"
                                                title="@RipHint(dig)"
                                                @onclick="() => RipItUp(dig)">@SpaceSails.Core.RipAndBin.Glyph</button>
                                    }
                                </div>
                            }
                        </div>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <div class="satchel-empty">@SpaceSails.Core.SeatedSpread.NothingToWorkLine</div>
                    }
@* ── MARKUP ENDS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
}
